                <pb facs="0379" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg291"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dawson to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose correspondence
                    relative to Francisco Martinez, a Porto Rican, who was imprisoned without bail
                    at Macoris, under circumstances which convinced the consular agent and myself
                    that it was more an attempt to collect a debt than a bona fide effort to punish
                    a crime.</p>
                <p>Upon representation being made, he was promptly released (August 5) on bail by
                    the Dominican Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>









